rl":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/deployments","created_at":"2026-08-05T16:00:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T17:31:44Z","pushed_at":"2026-09-23T18:02:56Z","git_url":"git://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF","homepage":"http://agentfield.ai/","size":196153,"stargazers_count":116,"watchers_count":116,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":14,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":141,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["agent-fleet","agent-harness","agentfield","agentic-coding","ai","ai-coding","cli-agent","coding-agent","coding-agents","coding-assistant","coding-cli","coding-harness","developer-tools","harness","harness-engineering","llm","open-models","open-source-models","software-factory","terminal-agent"],"visibility":"public","forks":14,"open_issues":141,"watchers":116,"default_branch":"dev","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pulls/1331","html_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1331","diff_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1331.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1331.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"A task that ended `failed` with its work still held wore `your call` and counted\ntoward `needs you` for the rest of the session. Nothing was waiting on any of\nthose answers.\n\nCloses #1328.\n\n## The engine already says this, in two places the reading disagreed with\n\n`internal/session/task_landing_question.go` raises a landing question for\n`TaskUnverified` and retires it for every other state. A failed node therefore\nhas no question object and never had one: no turn is parked on it, and no\nconversation is holding it.\n\n`Agent.handToModelOnAuto` writes a decider only for `TaskUnverified`, and its\ncomment says why in terms that settle this one:\n\n> AND IT IS ONLY EVER ABOUT THE ONE STATE THAT HAS A DECISION IN IT. A node that\n> landed done, incomplete or stopped is not waiting on anybody's word, and\n> writing an owner onto it would invent a question nobody is asking.\n\n`taskLifecycleStatus` gave that same node `TaskPresenceNeedsLook`, which becomes\n`Attention`, which is a demand. Two readers of one state, and the fix is to make\nthe reading agree with the law already written rather than to add a third\nopinion.\n\nTHE ROW STOPS ASSERTING A WAITER THAT DOES NOT EXIST.\n\n## What changed, and what deliberately did not\n\n`taskStatusDemand` now takes the facts, and one predicate turns `Attention` off\nfor a failed held landing a person did not stop.\n\nThe card is untouched, and that is the point. The tier, the word, the reason and\nboth answers all stay: the branch is on disk, taking it anyway is a real thing\nto do, and a person who goes looking at the row is owed the offer. What goes is\nonly `TaskStatus.Attention`, which is what files a row under `needs you`.\n\nIt is the same separation, for the same reason, that `internal/tui3`'s\n`taskstatus.go` already makes for a question somebody else is holding: \"The\ntier, the word and the question are untouched: the row still wears the `?` and\nstill reads its reason, because a person watching it is owed both.\"\n\nNo new field, no owner written, no clock, no count, no graph walk, no disk read.\n\n## It does not delete the demand\n\nIt moves it back to whoever has one. If something in a conversation ever does\nneed this answer to carry on, it ASKS, and an ask raises the mark through its\nown lane in `Agent.waitingOnPerson` with no help from this row. A held landing\nwill not wear the mark as the engine stands, because nothing ever waits on one\ntoday; wire a real park onto that answer and it marks again, through the ask\nlane, with no further change here.\n\n## Three candidate signals that were rejected, with the reason\n\nThe issue asks what \"moved past it\" should be measured against. None of the\nthree it names can answer it.\n\nA LATER NODE THAT LANDED THE SAME BRANCH cannot happen. A branch is\n`task/<slug>-<shortID>` and `shortID` is three bytes of `crypto/rand`, so no two\nnodes ever share a branch name. A predicate on it could never be true and a test\nfor it could never fail.\n\nA CONTINUATION LEAVES NO SECOND NODE. `task_continue.go` re-arms the node in\nplace: same id, same spec, same tree. A new proposal is explicitly a different\npiece of work, with no recorded link. There is no supersession edge to read.\n\nA BRANCH THAT NO LONGER EXISTS needs a disk probe on the road that draws every\ncard, which is exactly a claim the notice does not carry.\n\nA static `dependsOn` edge was considered and rejected too: it says what COULD\nwait, not what IS waiting, so it would still raise a mark at the moment of\nfailure for any task with a dependent.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nNew file `internal/session/task_held_mark_test.go`.\n\nOn `e87b147c9` as it stands:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestAHeldLandingOffersTheAnswerAndDemandsNothing\n    a held landing stands in `needs you` with nothing waiting on the answer\n```\n\nWith the change, `ok`. The red is the base's: `task_status.go` was checked out\nto the index to produce it and then restored, rather than the change being\nmutated.\n\nTHE TEST HAS CONTROLS, because a test that only asserts nothing demands anything\nwould pass on a reading that stopped demanding everything.\n`TestTheRowsSomethingIsWaitingOnStillDemand` pins three rows that still set\n`Attention`, each with something genuinely on the other side of the answer: a\nconflict, which is two versions of the person's own files and only they can say\nwhich survives; a landing nobody could check; and work nothing is driving. A\nthird test pins that a person's own stop is OVER and grows no question, since\nboth settle `failed` and the new predicate must not be what keeps a stopped row\nquiet.\n\nThe existing held-landing cases in `task_states_test.go` pin the card for\nexactly these facts, tier `your call`, `accept anyway` and `not right`, owner\nperson. They still pass, which is the evidence the card survived rather than an\nassertion that it did.\n\n## Checks\n\nWritten against `e87b147c9`, and the red above was re-verified on that head\nrather than carried over from the earlier base.\n\n```\nok  \tgithub.com/Agent-Field/codeaf/internal/session\t252.706s\nok  \tgithub.com/Agent-Field/codeaf/internal/tui3\t331.603s\n```\n\nBoth under the box's one heavy-suite lock, in one run, with `-count=1`.\n`internal/tui3` is in it because that is where `Attention` is read, and a change\nto the mark checked only in `internal/session` is checked in the wrong place.\n\n`bash scripts/laws.sh` exits 0. `gofmt -l ./cmd ./internal` prints nothing.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1331/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1331/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":31501979732,"node_id":"REFE_lADOTu5AHM8AAAABSSMoKM8AAAAHVaoQVA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/events/31501979732","actor":{"login":"santoshkumarradha","id":29346072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzQ2MDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29346072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha","html_url":"https://github.com/santoshkumarradha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"referenced","commit_id":"eeadf6a89461c63ec6680fa259e79f774d14ed51","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/commits/eeadf6a89461c63ec6680fa259e79f774d14ed51","created_at":"2026-09-21T03:16:56Z","performed_via_github_app":null}]